{"step_index":472,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-24T18:16:35Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-24T23:46:35+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-10-24T23:46:35+05:30\nShowing lines 1-157 of 157\n1: # HackerRank Orchestrate - October 2026\n2: \n3: ## Ghost Data Still Exists\n4: \n5: Build an AI agent that audits whether a user's personal data was actually deleted.\n6: \n7: A deletion workflow may report **Complete** while data still exists in databases, logs, support attachments, exports, search indexes, archives, or backups. Sync and restore processes may also bring deleted data back.\n8: \n9: For each request, the agent must first determine whether deletion was actually requested. It then returns `COMPLETE`, `INCOMPLETE`, or `NOT_APPLICABLE`, reports any remaining data or recreation risk, and produces the ordered remediation and verification steps required to finish an authorized deletion safely.\n10: \n11: Read [`problem_statement.md`](./problem_statement.md) for the complete challenge contract.\n12: \n13: ---\n14: \n15: ## Quick Start\n16: \n17: Clone the repository and move into the project directory:\n18: \n19: ```bash\n20: git clone https://github.com/interviewstreet/hackerrank-orchestrate-october26.git\n21: cd hackerrank-orchestrate-october26\n22: ```\n23: \n24: Start your AI coding tool from the **repository root** so it automatically reads [`AGENTS.md`](./AGENTS.md) and logs your session turns to `log.txt` in the root directory.\n25: \n26: Build your solution in `code/main.py`, or use another language and document its setup and run command clearly in your README.\n27: \n28: Your solution must:\n29: \n30: - Read the input files from `dataset/`\n31: - Generate one prediction row for every request in `dataset/deletion_requests.csv`\n32: - Write the final predictions to `output.csv` in the repository root\n33: \n34: Run the starter Python entry point with:\n35: \n36: ```bash\n37: python3 code/main.py\n38: ```\n39: \n40: The blank template at `dataset/output.csv` is provided as a reference. Your final generated file for submission must be the root-level `output.csv`.\n41: \n42: \n43: ## Dataset\n44: \n45: All participant-facing files are in\n<truncated 5071 bytes>\neval approach. Include clear setup and execution instructions in `README.md` inside `code.zip`.\n128: \n129: To package `code.zip` from the repository root without bundling the dataset:\n130: \n131: **macOS / Linux:**\n132: \n133: ```bash\n134: zip -r code.zip README.md code -x \"*/__pycache__/*\" \"*/.venv/*\" \"*/venv/*\" \"*/node_modules/*\" \"*/.git/*\" \"*/.DS_Store\"\n135: ```\n136: \n137: **Windows (PowerShell):**\n138: \n139: ```powershell\n140: Compress-Archive -Path README.md, code -DestinationPath code.zip -Force\n141: ```\n142: \n143: When packaging `code.zip`:\n144: \n145: - Keep your evaluation reports in `code/evaluation/` so they are bundled automatically with `code` (or add `evaluation` to the archive command above if you placed them in a top-level `evaluation/` directory).\n146: - Do **not** include `dataset/`, virtual environments (`.venv`, `venv`, `node_modules`), or build caches (`__pycache__`). On Windows, keep `.venv` at the repository root (outside `code/`) and remove any `code/__pycache__` folders before running `Compress-Archive`.\n147: - Do **not** include nested archives (`.zip`, `.tar`, `.gz`, `.tgz`, `.7z`, `.rar`) inside `code.zip` — submissions containing nested archive files will be rejected.\n148: \n149: Before submitting, confirm that:\n150: \n151: - `output.csv` has the exact header `case_id,deletion_status,steps_json` and contains all 518 data rows sorted by `case_id`;\n152: - every `steps_json` value is a valid JSON array with consecutive step numbers starting at `1`;\n153: - findings cite valid evidence IDs, and `COMPLETE` verification steps cite evidence proving the current state;\n154: - proposed remediation and future verification steps use an empty `evidence_id` (`\"\"`);\n155: - `code.zip` includes your runnable code, `README.md`, `code/evaluation/evaluation_report.md`, and `code/evaluation/usage_report.md`;\n156: - `log.txt` follows the `AGENTS.md` turn format and is uploaded to the `chat_transcript` slot; and\n157: - no API keys, credentials, real personal data, or sensitive configuration values are included.","truncated_fields":["content"]}
